      "writtenOn": "2021-07-06T19:31:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "probably not something to fix in this CL,\n\nbut I think this function should actually take the timeout to set (ie. number of seconds).\n\nin the lastused was updated case, we should actually be doing\n\ntimeout we want - (now - lastUsed)\n\nso that if it was lastUsed 5 seconds ago, the timeout we set is 5 seconds smaller.\n\n--\n\nalternatively the function could take a \u0027timeout offset\u0027, ie. relative to how many seconds ago to set the timeout.\n\nhere you\u0027d pass 0, and set to 432000 - 0,\nbut in the udp update case you\u0027d pass now - lastUsed, and set to udpTimeout - arg",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1621,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 1621,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "a937967033d6fa3895d8700103832376d5a2fd8d",
